// =============================================================================
// Maths Duel Arena — cosmetics (spec §6.3)
//
// Every cosmetic the game knows, for sale or not. The player equips one of
// each kind: an avatar, a profile banner, a style of answer buttons, an
// arena background and an effect on right answers.
//   "price": 0      owned from the start (each kind but titles needs one)
//   "price": N      sold in the shop for N gems
//                   Prices climb steeply: a few hundred gems for the
//                   first ones (weeks of play), thousands for the rarest
//                   (months; see bin/simulate.dart for gems per day)
//   no "price"      earned only: a world perk (worlds.jsonc) or an
//                   achievement (achievements.jsonc) grants it
// Looks (colours are "#RRGGBB"):
//   avatar      "icon" (person, rocket, bolt, brain, pets, flame, star,
//               diamond, calculate, crown, planet, music) on a gradient of
//               two "colors"
//   banner      a gradient of two "colors" with a "pattern" (plain,
//               stripes, dots, waves)
//   buttons     the answer buttons' "colors" (one) and "shape" (rounded,
//               pill, sharp); the free one keeps the buttons as designed
//   background  the arena's glow, "colors" (one); the free one keeps each
//               screen's own glow
//   effect      the burst on a right answer: "burst" (sparks, stars,
//               confetti, lightning, digits, fireworks, supernova) in 1
//               to 4 "colors"
//   (Titles are no longer cosmetics: every achievement is a badge that
//   can be shown on the profile banner; see achievements.jsonc.)
//   "pass": true  given by the Arena Pass, one a month: the look of that month
//               ("month": 1–12) first, else the next in catalog order
//               (never sold, no price)
//   "rarity"    common, rare, epic or legendary (default common): rare
//               avatars get a metal ring; epic ones a turning ring and
//               banners a shimmer; legendary ones sparkles and a glow too
//   Banners may also use the patterns grid, stars, equations, circuit and
//   aurora; buttons a "finish" (outline, gradient with two colours,
//   glass, neon, and the legendary gold and platinum, which shine);
//   backgrounds a "scene" (glow, stars, aurora, digits, bubbles, storm). Boss trophies are legendary, earned only.
//   "trophy"    a world id: an avatar or banner its ultimate boss grants,
//               drawn as the world's sign on a rainbow (no colours)
// Names are in the app's translations (one per id). Booster prices and
// limits are in balance.jsonc → economy.
// =============================================================================
{
  "version": 1,
  "cosmetics": [
